WEBVTT

00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:14,580
What does it mean when you have an increase in bilirubin?

00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:24,900
So, bilirubin is a, shows a function of your liver, really.

00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:30,700
So, bilirubin is, when you get your bilirubin measured in your blood,

00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:37,100
if you could have a total bilirubin or you could have an indirect bilirubin.

00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:46,340
So, you're, typically, your total bilirubin is composed of, what's called your indirect bilirubin.

00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:51,340
Your indirect bilirubin is also called your un-pagigated bilirubin.

00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:57,140
And that circulates in your blood on the way to the liver.

00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:02,380
And then you have direct or conjugated bilirubin.

00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:09,100
And that is, when your liver makes the bilirubin water soluble to be deposited in the bile,

00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:16,100
to be then go through the bile duct in the gallbladder and in the, in the small intestine.

00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:26,780
Remember, your bile is what brings all the toxins from your liver down into your small intestine as well.

00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:32,540
That your bile also contains lipase to help break down fats.

00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:37,580
So, but bilirubin is the breakdown of hemoglobin.

00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:45,060
So, when you have an increased bilirubin, it can be because you have a breakdown in hemoglobin.

00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:52,980
So, you can have a breakdown in the blood disorder where you have what's called hemolysis,

00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:57,220
where you have a breakdown in red blood cells in the blood.

00:01:57,220 --> 00:02:00,700
That's less common.

00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:08,260
Most of the time when you see an increase in bilirubin, it's because of a blockage of the bile duct.

00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:15,540
So, remember, your bilirubin will ultimately go through the liver and become made water soluble in the liver

00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:20,340
and then go through in the bile to the small intestine.

00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:24,140
That is the most common, especially for a person who has cancer,

00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:28,500
when a person has increased bilirubin, you're concerned with a blocked bile duct.

00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:33,220
Now, you can have a blocked bile duct for multiple reasons.

00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:38,540
With a, with a diagnosed cancer, you're concerned with metastasis to the liver

00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:43,060
and then a space-occupied lesion pinching the bile duct.

00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:47,460
There's other possible reasons for a blocked bile duct.

00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:55,780
But that's what the biggest thing you'd be concerned with having a current cancer diagnosis is a blocked bile duct.

